# =============================================================================

# ArXiv MCP Server - Enterprise .gitignore Configuration

# =============================================================================

# This file follows enterprise patterns for clean repository management

# and workspace organization according to Diátaxis documentation framework.

# =============================================================================

# I. ENTERPRISE DEVELOPMENT ARTIFACTS (.dev/ directory)

# =============================================================================

# All development artifacts are consolidated under .dev/ for clean separation

# This includes build outputs, caches, logs, tools, and temporary files

# Development directory (enterprise organization)

# Entire development workspace (default ignored)
.dev/

# Allow permanent high-value documentation inside .dev/docs/
!.dev/docs/
!.dev/docs/**

# Granular .dev/ patterns for better control (if needed for exceptions)

.dev/artifacts/ # Build artifacts and outputs
.dev/build/ # Compiled code and distributions
.dev/cache/ # All cache types (network, dependency, etc.)
.dev/runtime/ # Runtime logs, PIDs, and temporary data
.dev/temp/ # Temporary files and scratch space
.dev/tools/coverage/ # Coverage reports (HTML, XML, etc.)

# Legacy cache directories (now symlinked to .dev/cache/)

# These patterns ensure old cache references are still ignored

arxiv_cache/
batch_cache/
dependency_cache/
network_cache/
notification_cache/
reading_cache/
tag_cache/
trending_cache/

# =============================================================================

# II. PYTHON ECOSYSTEM ARTIFACTS

# =============================================================================

# Python bytecode and compiled files

__pycache__/
**.py[cod]
**.pyo
**.pyd
**$py.class

# Distribution and packaging

build/
dist/
wheels/
**.egg-info/
**.egg
.eggs/
.Python
develop-eggs/
downloads/
eggs/
lib/
lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
.installed.cfg
MANIFEST

# Package management

uv.lock # UV lock file (tracked in production, ignored in dev)
pip-wheel-metadata/
pip-log.txt
pip-delete-this-directory.txt

# Virtual environments

.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
env.bak/
venv.bak/

# Environment configuration

.python-version
.env
.env.**
.env.local
.env.development
.env.production
.env.test

# =============================================================================

# III. TESTING AND QUALITY ASSURANCE

# =============================================================================

# Test execution artifacts

.pytest_cache/
.tox/
.nox/
.hypothesis/

# Coverage reports (prefer .dev/tools/coverage/ for organized storage)

.coverage
.coverage.**
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
**.cover
**.py,cover
nosetests.xml

# Type checking and linting

.mypy_cache/
.dmypy.json
dmypy.json
.pyre/
.pytype/

# Performance and benchmarking

.benchmarks/

# =============================================================================

# IV. IDE AND DEVELOPMENT TOOLS

# =============================================================================

# Visual Studio Code

.vscode/
!.vscode/settings.json # Allow shared VS Code settings
!.vscode/tasks.json # Allow shared tasks
!.vscode/launch.json # Allow shared debug configs

# JetBrains IDEs

.idea/
**.iml
**.iws

# Vim/Neovim

**.swp
**.swo
**~
.netrwhist

# Emacs

*~
#*#
.#**

# Sublime Text

**.sublime-workspace
**.sublime-project

# Rope (Python refactoring tool)

.ropeproject

# Spyder

.spyderproject
.spyproject

# =============================================================================

# V. OPERATING SYSTEM ARTIFACTS

# =============================================================================

# macOS

.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
.*_**
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride

# Windows

Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
ehthumbs_vista.db
**.stackdump
[Dd]esktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# Linux

.fuse_hidden**
.directory
.Trash-**
.nfs**

# =============================================================================

# VI. VERSION CONTROL AND CI/CD

# =============================================================================

# Git-specific

.git/
.gitconfig
.gitmodules

# GitHub Actions artifacts (allow workflow files)

.github/.knowledge_base # Keep knowledge base private to repo
!.github/workflows/ # Allow workflow files

# CI/CD artifacts

.coverage
junit.xml
test-results/

# =============================================================================

# VII. DOCUMENTATION AND CONTENT

# =============================================================================

# Documentation build outputs

docs/*_build/
docs/.doctrees/
site/
.mkdocs/

# Jupyter Notebook

.ipynb_checkpoints/
**.ipynb_checkpoints

# =============================================================================

# VIII. WORKSPACE ORGANIZATION ENFORCEMENT

# =============================================================================

# These patterns prevent file scatter and enforce enterprise organization

# Prevent development scripts in root (should be in .dev/tools/)

/debug*_*.py
/test*_*.py
/**_debug.py
/*_test.py
/tool_*.py
/*_tool.py
/validate_*.py
/fix*_*.py

# Prevent scattered documentation

/TODO*_*.md
/TASKS*_*.md
/NOTES*_*.md
/DRAFT*_*.md

# Prevent cache scatter (should be in .dev/cache/)

/**_cache/
/cache*/
/temp**/

# Prevent log scatter (should be in .dev/runtime/logs/)

/*.log
/logs/
/log*/

# =============================================================================

# IX. APPLICATION-SPECIFIC ARTIFACTS

# =============================================================================

# ArXiv MCP specific outputs

output/ # ArXiv download outputs
network_cache/ # Network request cache
nonexistent/ # Placeholder directories

# Database files

**.db
***.db-shm
**.db-wal
**.sqlite
**.sqlite3
dump.rdb

# Compiled extensions

**.so
**.dylib
**.dll

# Temporary files

tmp/
temp/
**.tmp
**.temp
**.bak
**.backup

# Archive files (unless specifically needed)

**.zip
**.tar.gz
**.tar.bz2
**.tar.xz
**.7z

# =============================================================================

# X. SECURITY AND SECRETS

# =============================================================================

# Secrets and sensitive configuration

secrets.json
config.json
**.key
**.pem
**.p12
**.crt
**.csr
**.pfx

# Authentication tokens

.netrc
auth.json
token.txt

# =============================================================================

# XI. PROJECT-SPECIFIC EXCEPTIONS (Use negation patterns sparingly)

# =============================================================================

# Example: Allow specific config files that should be tracked

# !config/example.yaml

# !.github/workflows/

# =============================================================================

# END OF ENTERPRISE .gitignore CONFIGURATION

# =============================================================================
